  "subdivision_of_building": "Rear ground floor external terrace",
  "status": "Application Received",
  "description": "The proposal seeks to upgrade the existing terrace to provide a more accessible, functional, and visually coherent external space while respecting the site’s context, being situated within a designated Conservation Area in the London Borough of Camden.\n\nThe works include the removal of the existing paving and the installation of a raised‑floor pedestal system to support new paving tiles and bonded gravel. This construction method eliminates the need for steps and allows for the formation of gentle, compliant gradients, significantly improving accessibility. The raised system has also been selected to protect the extensive root structure of the existing willow tree on site. By avoiding excavation and allowing air and water to continue to reach the root zone, the design ensures that the tree’s health and long‑term growth are not compromised.\n\nIn addition, the proposal includes the replacement of the existing balustrade railings. The new balustrade will match the design and appearance of the adjacent railing located across the canal, enhancing visual continuity and contributing positively to the character of the Conservation Area.",
